flowchart LR
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: competitive bidding is the general rule. Which other modes does the law allow, and for what kind of situation is each one meant?
  %% READING: left = the kind of situation. Right = the mode. The order of the modes follows sections 26 to 37 of the Act.
  %% SOURCES: the names and the number of the modes [RA12009 ss.26-37][IRR12009 s.26.1]. The mode must be stated in the Annual Procurement Plan [RA12009 s.7]. The conditions and amounts of each mode are from sections 27 to 37 of the Implementing Rules, in the text published on 10 February 2025 [IRR12009]. The committee for bids may delegate modes 5 to 11 to the end-user unit or the procurement unit [IRR12009 s.26.4]. Common-use supplies are bought only from the Procurement Service, when it has them [IRR12009 s.40.1]. Splitting of a contract to stay below a threshold is prohibited [IRR12009 s.39].
  %% LIMIT: the lines give the main condition only. The thirteen cases of negotiated procurement are listed in chapter E1, section 2.7. Do not rely on this diagram for a legal decision on the mode.
  %% AFTER THE RULES: the Rules let the GPPB add a type of negotiated procurement under four conditions [IRR12009 s.35]. The GPPB added one on 7 January 2026, for international events that the government hosts [GPPB2026-01]. Guidelines of 25 September 2025 name one more mode of negotiation, for agricultural and fishery products from accredited cooperatives and enterprises of farmers and fisherfolk [GPPB2025-08]. Guidelines of 15 January 2026 give the steps of mode 11 [GPPB2026-04]. I read these three documents as summaries with short quotations.
  %% THIS IS NOT THE DECISION TREE OF THE GPPB: on 25 November 2025 the GPPB adopted a decision tree for the choice of the mode, as a guide and as an annex of the Rules [GPPB2025-12]. I did not see that tree. This diagram is my own arrangement of the modes.

  S(["One line of the<br/>Annual Procurement Plan"]) --> Q{"What is the<br/>situation?"}

  Q -- "general rule" --> M1["1  COMPETITIVE BIDDING<br/>open to all eligible bidders (see E1-b)"]:::main
  Q -- "few known suppliers of a<br/>specialized item" --> M2["2  LIMITED SOURCE BIDDING<br/>invitation to pre-selected suppliers: highly specialized goods or<br/>consulting from few sources, major plant components,<br/>specialized works that affect national security"]
  Q -- "the agency cannot yet<br/>define the solution" --> M3["3  COMPETITIVE DIALOGUE<br/>two stages, for innovative or complex needs and for<br/>specifications that cannot be defined in advance"]
  Q -- "a private party offers a<br/>new concept or technology" --> M4["4  UNSOLICITED OFFER WITH BID MATCHING<br/>the agency invites competing bids, and the<br/>first offeror may match the best one"]
  Q -- "only one source exists" --> M5["5  DIRECT CONTRACTING<br/>goods only: proprietary item, critical component from one<br/>source, or exclusive dealer with no cheaper sub-dealer"]
  Q -- "readily available item<br/>of small amount" --> M6["6  DIRECT ACQUISITION<br/>contract budget up to PHP 200,000, from a registered<br/>supplier, an online shop or an item sold ready for use"]
  Q -- "more of the same item from<br/>the last winning bidder" --> M7["7  REPEAT ORDER<br/>same or lower unit price, within 6 months of the notice to<br/>proceed, at most 25 percent of the first quantity"]
  Q -- "amount below a threshold" --> M8["8  SMALL VALUE PROCUREMENT<br/>contract budget up to PHP 2,000,000 (lower for smaller local<br/>governments, PHP 100,000 for a barangay). Request for quotations"]
  Q -- "failed biddings, emergency,<br/>and other listed cases" --> M9["9  NEGOTIATED PROCUREMENT<br/>thirteen cases listed in the Rules, among them: two failed biddings, emergency,<br/>take-over of an ended contract, adjacent work, another agency,<br/>lease of real property and venue, fuel and online subscriptions.<br/>The GPPB may add a type. Added on 7 January 2026:<br/>international events that the government hosts"]
  Q -- "the supplier sold<br/>the same item to<br/>another agency" --> M10["10  DIRECT SALES<br/>an item that is not a common-use supply, from a supplier that delivered<br/>the same item to another agency under a contract awarded by bidding:<br/>within 6 months from that acceptance, at the same or a lower unit price"]
  Q -- "research, development<br/>and innovation needs" --> M11["11  DIRECT PROCUREMENT FOR SCIENCE,<br/>TECHNOLOGY AND INNOVATION<br/>supplies for research and development,<br/>commissioned goods, purchases from startups"]

